---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="What Agent Skills are, how to install them from skills.merze.ai, and how to contribute."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
>
  <article class="prose about-page">
    <h1>About Agent Skills</h1>
    <p>
      Agent Skills are folders of instructions that coding agents can load on
      demand. Each skill is a directory with a <code>SKILL.md</code> file
      (YAML frontmatter + markdown body) and optional supporting files.
    </p>

    <h2>Install a skill</h2>
    <p>
      Open any skill in the catalog and use the download or copy actions on the
      detail page:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Download <code>SKILL.md</code> (and any supporting files) from this
        site.
      </li>
      <li>
        Place them in your agent’s skills directory as
        <code>&lt;slug&gt;/SKILL.md</code>.
      </li>
      <li>Reload or restart the agent so it discovers the new skill.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Domain-based install routes (for example
      <code>/skill/&lt;name&gt;</code>) are planned separately and are not part
      of this catalog yet.
    </p>

    <h2>Contribute a skill</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Create a folder at the repo root named with the skill slug
        (lowercase letters, digits, and hyphens; max 64 characters).
      </li>
      <li>
        Add <code>SKILL.md</code> with required frontmatter:
        <ul>
          <li><code>name</code> — must match the folder name</li>
          <li><code>description</code> — 1–1024 characters</li>
          <li>
            Optional <code>metadata.version</code>, <code>source</code>,
            <code>category</code>, <code>tags</code>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li>Open a pull request to <code>main</code>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      This site rebuilds from every root <code>*/SKILL.md</code>. Invalid
      <code>name</code> or <code>description</code>, or a name/folder mismatch,
      fails the build.
    </p>

    <h2>Merze</h2>
    <p>
      Skills are published by
      <a href="https://merze.ai">Merze</a>. Questions or contributions are
      welcome through the usual review process for this catalog.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
